DESCRIPTION:<span>Step aside Windows and get out of the way macOS\, it's ti
 me to learn about linux!  Linux is used on all of the CS lab machines\, and
  it will be essential for many of your classes. As with all of our events\,
  we welcome anyone to attend even if you've never been to an ACM event befo
 re.</span><br><span> <br>CS101s are ACM's interactive lecture series where 
 you'll learn useful industry standard tools that don't get taught in classe
 s. If you've heard about MIT's Missing Semester class\, that is what we're 
 emulating here. Our lectures are aimed primarily for freshmen but even expe
 rienced developers will learn new things at our sessions! <span><p>Learn mo
 re at:<br><a href="https://texasacm.org/">https://texasacm.org/</a><br><a h
 ref="https://instagram.com/texas_acm">https://instagram.com/texas_acm</a><b
 r><a href="https://discord.gg/gVuUcuH">https://discord.gg/gVuUcuH</a></p></
 span></span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230808T144334Z
LOCATION:GDC 2.506
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ACM CS101 #2: Linux Tech Tips!
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
