CREATED:20230507T195707Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>It's registration time! ACM might not be able to get you int
 o the classes you want\, but we can help you decide which classes to try fo
 r. Enjoy a fresh stack of pancakes as you chat with professors 1-on-1 about
  their classes so you can decide if you're interested and ask key questions
  before you register. <br><br>As with all of our events\, we welcome anyone
  to attend even if you've never been to an ACM event before. Professors in 
 attendance TBA -- check our Discord for the most up-to-date information!<br
 ><br>Learn more at:<br><a href="https://texasacm.org/">https://texasacm.org
 /</a><br><a href="https://instagram.com/texas_acm">https://instagram.com/te
 xas_acm</a><br><a href="https://discord.gg/gVuUcuH">https://discord.gg/gVuU
 cuH</a> <br></p>\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/jzp-xvmv
 -xrf\nOr dial: (US) +1 636-306-2098 PIN: 304729335#\nMore phone numbers: ht
 tps://tel.meet/jzp-xvmv-xrf?pin=3651952813577&hs=7\n\nLearn more about Meet
  at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720
LAST-MODIFIED:20240404T230725Z
LOCATION:GDC 1.304
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CS411 Pancakes and Professors
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20240118T233000Z
DTEND:20240119T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261124T200004Z
UID:50t37eos2ptsqn9ci8o1s7e2hl@google.com
CREATED:20230507T193305Z
DESCRIPTION:Grab a bite to eat and learn about ACM at our spring kickoff! A
 nyone interested in computing is welcome to join our community. We hope to 
 see you there!<p> Upcoming Events:<br></p><p>Friday\, 01/19 <b>CS101 #1 - L
 inux Tech TIps</b>: <span>This interactive lecture series teaches you usefu
 l industry standard tools that don't get taught in classes. Our Linux lectu
 re will be especially helpful for incoming CS429 students!</span></p><p><sp
 an>Monday\, 01/22 <b>Paycom Hack Night</b>:</span> Work on a personal proje
 ct and meet some Paycom engineers! Hack nights are like casual\, mini hacka
 thons--ACM provides the food and dedicated space (and prizes!) and you brin
 g fun project ideas. Free food for all attendees!</p><p>Tuesday\, 01/23 <b>
 Paycom Gaming Night</b>: Bring your A-game to ACM's Paycom gaming night! We
 'll have board games\, card games\, video games\, and probably any other ga
 me you can think of so you can get to know Paycom recruiters and engineers 
 in a casual setting. </p><p>Monday\, 01/29 <b>Guest Speaker Event</b>:  Dr.
  Mark Ravina is a professor of Japanese digital humanities and works with d
 igital mapping and the history of cartography. <br></p><p><b>Coffee Chats</
 b>: We want to provide an informal setting for freshmen to engage in meanin
 gful conversations and gain valuable insights. Chats will introduce student
 s to our programs\, and help develop the informal connections that are cruc
 ial to success here at UT &amp\; beyond. If it also helps you feed your caf
 feine addiction for free\, that's an added bonus!<br></p><p>About ACM:<br>T
 he Association for Computing Machinery is a UT chapter of the national ACM.
  We put on social\, academic\, and professional events. ACM is also a commu
 nity of people enthusiastic about any and all aspects of computing. Anyone 
 interested in computing is welcome to join. It's a great place to make frie
 nds or learn from other students!</p><p>Learn more at:<br><a href="https://
 texasacm.org/">https://texasacm.org/</a><br><a href="https://instagram.com/
 texas_acm">https://instagram.com/texas_acm</a><br><a href="https://discord.
 gg/gVuUcuH">https://discord.gg/gVuUcuH</a></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240114T220435Z
LOCATION:GDC 2.216
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ACM Spring Kickoff
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
