 nts\, ask them questions\, and interact with them in their native habitat (
 in the proximity of coffee). Now you have a chance to speak to some of the 
 people who review your applications and see what they are looking for in a 
 grad school applicant. <br> <br>Panelists include Etienne Vouga (Graphics)\
 , Amy Pavel (Human-Computer Interaction)\, and Eunsol Choi (NLP).<br> <br><
 span><span><span>Learn more at:<br><a href="https://texasacm.org/">https://
 texasacm.org/</a><br><a href="https://instagram.com/texas_acm">https://inst
 agram.com/texas_acm</a><br><a href="https://discord.gg/gVuUcuH">https://dis
 cord.gg/gVuUcuH</a></span></span></span>\n\nJoin with Google Meet: https://
 meet.google.com/bxo-bewm-tbj\nOr dial: (US) +1 401-646-2311 PIN: 148072180#
 \nMore phone numbers: https://tel.meet/bxo-bewm-tbj?pin=5282638616557&hs=7\
 n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282
 720
