UID:7r4qh55i36borktj896he61ega@google.com
CREATED:20230507T195132Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Someone call the Docker\, we have a deployment emergency on 
 our hands! If you've ever been in a situation where you've had to juggle di
 fferent Python versions\, Java versions\, versions! versions! versions! you
  may need to try learning how to use Docker. Docker lets you run your code 
 in different environments without ever having to say- uhhhhh\, it runs on m
 y machine but not yours…!? <br></p><p>If you’ve ever been in a situation wh
 ere an interviewer asks about your Docker experience and you have to hem an
 d haw\, this event is for you! ACM will give you the introduction you need 
 to start using it to simplify your workflow and make your applications port
 able. Reject operating systems\, embrace containers!</p><p><br></p><p><span
 ><span><span><span>Learn more at:<br><a href="https://texasacm.org/">https:
 //texasacm.org/</a><br><a href="https://instagram.com/texas_acm">https://in
 stagram.com/texas_acm</a><br><a href="https://discord.gg/gVuUcuH">https://d
 iscord.gg/gVuUcuH</a></span></span> </span></span></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240229T143922Z
LOCATION:GDC 5.304
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CS101: Docker Do's and Don'ts
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
