BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20240304T230000Z
DTEND:20240305T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261124T200004Z
UID:1a3999ru8k72fi3dbi0082fqd6@google.com
CREATED:20240205T234841Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Don't freak out. Did you know that most systems we use today
  are <em>wildly</em> insecure? This past year attackers have exploited bugs
  in systems like browsers and operating systems to steal user data\, shut d
 own hospitals\, and stalk activists. Attackers are winning because bugs in 
 a seemingly unimportant component like the browser's spell-checker can be u
 sed to compromise the entire browser.<br> <br>In this talk\, Shravan will d
 escribe his work retrofitting existing systems towards secure design. First
 \, he will describe RLBox\, a type-driven novel sandboxing framework that i
 s an integral part of the Firefox browser. RLBox helps Firefox engineers re
 trofit the browser to sandbox third-party libraries and safeguard its users
  from attacks that exploit vulnerabilities from these libraries. Then he wi
 ll describe his work on the VeriWasm analysis tool and Swivel compiler whic
 h together secure edge cloud platforms against attacks that exploit compile
 r bugs and micro-architectural vulnerabilities like Spectre. Along the way\
 , he will describe the challenges and research questions that only arise wh
 en trying to deploy principles techniques (e.g.\, from programming language
 s and system design) to secure huge systems like Firefox.<br></p><p>This wi
 ll be a talk to attend for anyone interested in the challenges of securing 
 real-world systems and preventing microarchitecture attacks! Dinner and des
 sert will be provided.<br></p><p><br></p><p>Learn more at:<br><a href="http
 s://texasacm.org/">https://texasacm.org/</a><br><a href="https://instagram.
 com/texas_acm">https://instagram.com/texas_acm</a><br><a href="https://disc
 ord.gg/gVuUcuH">https://discord.gg/gVuUcuH</a><br></p><p><br><br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240227T163814Z
LOCATION:GDC 1.304
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ISSS + ACM Talk - Shravan Narayan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
