CREATED:20230507T193323Z
DESCRIPTION:Linux is used on all of the CS lab machines\, and it will be es
 sential for many of your classes\, including CS 429! We've spoken with your
  429 TAs to help YOU figure out everything you need to get started working 
 on the Linux terminal. Pre and post-429 students are also welcome to come\,
  and there will be a little something to learn for everyone.<br><br>CS101s 
 are ACM's interactive lecture series where you'll learn useful industry sta
 ndard tools that don't get taught in classes. If you've heard about MIT's M
 issing Semester class\, that is what we're emulating here. Our lectures are
  aimed primarily for freshmen but even experienced developers will learn ne
 w things at our sessions!<br> <br>Learn more at:<br><a href="https://texasa
 cm.org/">https://texasacm.org/</a><br><a href="https://instagram.com/texas_
 acm">https://instagram.com/texas_acm</a><br><a href="https://discord.gg/gVu
 UcuH">https://discord.gg/gVuUcuH</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240115T033900Z
LOCATION:GDC 4.304
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CS101 #1: Linux Tech Tips
