CREATED:20250114T181415Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Grab a bite to eat and learn about ACM at our spring kickoff
 ! Anyone interested in computing is welcome to join our community. We hope 
 to see you there!</p><p>About ACM:<br>The Association for Computing Machine
 ry is a UT chapter of the national ACM. We put on social\, academic\, and p
 rofessional events. ACM is also a community of people enthusiastic about an
 y and all aspects of computing. Anyone interested in computing is welcome t
 o join. It's a great place to make friends or learn from other students!</p
 ><p>Learn more at:<br><a href="https://texasacm.org/">https://texasacm.org/
 </a><br><a href="https://instagram.com/texas_acm">https://instagram.com/tex
 as_acm</a><br><a href="https://discord.gg/gVuUcuH">https://discord.gg/gVuUc
 uH</a></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250114T181415Z
LOCATION:GDC 6.302
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Spring Kickoff
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20190412T223000Z
DTEND:20190413T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261124T200004Z
UID:722sdhdddcjaa0l2el0d73qfd8@google.com
CREATED:20180507T232551Z
DESCRIPTION:Come put your programming skills to the test! Whether you're ju
 st a beginner in 312 or you're a senior in your final semester there are qu
 estions for you! As always\, there will be free food!\n\nIn UT programming 
 competitions\, there are 5-7 problems. Each problem requires competitors to
  submit a program that can solve the problem. The winner is the person who 
 has solved the most problems. If multiple people have solved the same numbe
 r of problems\, the tiebreaker is the sum of the times it took to solve eac
 h problem\, in minutes. The top competitors win both great prizes and recog
 nition from Citadel Securities!
LAST-MODIFIED:20190401T142837Z
LOCATION:GDC 2.216
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Programming Competition
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
