DESCRIPTION:Grab a bite to eat and learn about ACM at our fall kickoff!  An
 yone interested in computing is welcome to join our community.  We hope to 
 see you there!<br><br>About ACM:<br>The Association for Computing Machinery
  is a UT chapter of the national ACM.  We put on social\, academic\, and pr
 ofessional events.  ACM is also a community of people enthusiastic about an
 y and all aspects of computing. Anyone interested in computing is welcome t
 o join.  It's a great place to make friends or learn from other students.<b
 r><br>Here are some of our events you can look forward to:<br>Gaming Night:
   Grab your friends and head up to the 6th floor to play boards games and v
 ideo games.<br>CS101: This interactive lecture series teaches you useful in
 dustry standard tools that don't get taught in classes.  We teach you how t
 o use git for class projects\, how to navigate the Linux lab machines\, and
  other useful development tools.<br>Sponsor Banquet:  Sit down and have din
 ner with recruiters and engineers from our sponsor companies.  This is your
  chance to ask about company life\, the interview process\, and internship/
 full time opportunities.<br>Learn more at: <br><a href="https://texasacm.or
 g/">https://texasacm.org/</a><br><a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/t
 exas.acm/">https://www.facebook.com/groups/texas.acm/</a><br><a href="https
 ://discord.gg/gVuUcuH">https://discord.gg/gVuUcuH</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230121T100957Z
